# 11. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS FOR TELEGRAM

- Keep `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` in `.env`.
- Never expose the bot token to Blade, JavaScript, browser HTML, Git, or public routes.
- Never expose the Telegram chat ID to employees if it is not necessary.
- Do not let public users send messages through the bot.
- Do not add Telegram login/authentication.
- Do not use Telegram as an approval authorization mechanism.
- The detail link must respect existing authentication/authorization.
- Sanitize dynamic user-provided strings before putting them into Telegram messages.
- Do not expose private attachment URLs in Telegram messages.

